        <p>This annual ceremony to-1 place at the Corege, Kenyon Hall on Tuesday. Captain T E Witlaington, J.P., presided, and Mrs Withineton presented the prizes,. There were also present :—Gr R Sephton, Mr S Sutton, of Warrington, and Mr John Suttol, of Culcheth College, and Mr and Mrs Granville, the principals. The proceed- ings were inaugurated by the presentation Of a bouquet to Mrs Withington by Master Cecil Kinsey. 'rho following programme was then gone through :—Physical exercises by the Misses Griffin, Crossley, Nina Warrington, Hilda Warrington, Elsie Gordon, Elsie Smith and A Harrison The drill was perfectly accomplished under the leadership of Miss ;Nina Warrington. (girls) and Master Harry P Sutton, (boys). Followingl this, were a pianoforte solo Irish Airs" Miss F Jones; mandoline solo " Scotch Airs," Miss M Crossley ; violin solo " Estudiantina" Miss L Brockmann ; mandoline duet "Black Bess" Misses Crossley and Collins ; pianoierte solo Master J C Sutton ; physical exercises by Mastere H Sutton, E Dean, W Scholes, C Wroe, H Wrce, and Hubert Sutton; song, Master C Taylor; mando:ine sob Master C Mellor.</p>
        <p>Mrs Withingtoo then distributed the pez:.,s as fol- lows :</p>
