        <p>Death of Mr. D. Knight, of Nantwich. Mr Daniel Knight, late manager of the " Guar- dian " Nantwich, died at, his residence Nantwich, shortly after two o'clock on Saturday afternoon, the immediate cause of death being acute peritoni- ti9. The deceased was the second son of the late Mr John Knight. engineer of Bath, and was born in that city in 1835. 11.0 served his apprenticeship on the " Bath Herald," and afterwards came to War- rington in 1863, and was engaged on the" Warring- ton Guardian," In 1868, under the late Dr Mackie he started the " Nantwich Guardian," and after- wards left to fill the position of chief reporter of the " Warrington Guardian." In 1875, he was appointed editor of the " Wigan Examiner," and on that occasion was the recipient of a very handsome testimonial from the inhabitant of the town where ' his services as editor were much appreciated. Pie left Wigan in 1876 and returned to Nantwich where he has been managing the " Guardian " ever since</p>
