        <p>IfiIIDDELEWRG, C...E COLONY, WEDNESDAY. Two rebels, turned Jacpbs and noste were executc .1 to-day.</p>
        <p>Promotion for a Warrington Volunteer</p>
        <p>Private Arthur It)gers, of 4, Fairseld-rlad, Stockton Heath, who is a member of the third coatigent of War. rington Volunteers, under Captain S Fairclough, in South Africa, has been veil:noted to Linc.-Corporal. In his last letter home he states that he was at the time stationed at Vryheid, and was in good health and spirits. More South Lancashires Ordered to</p>
