        <p>WARRINGTON PARISH CHURCH RESTORA- TION AND IMPROVEMENT FUND. An appeal has been issued for £3OOO for the Restoration and Improvement of the Parish Church. The parishioners haveall been Invited to contribute but it is believed that there are many outside the limits of the Old Parish who would recognize the claims of the mother Church upon them. Subscriptions from all such are earnestly solicited. The following amounts have been received or promised. £ 8. . Lord Lilford Hon Elinor Wilson-Patten Hon Elizabeth Wilson-Patton lOO Messrs Greenall Whitley and Co. lOO MeQsrs Walker and Co lOO Mr Isherwood " 6 Mr R T Fairelough 6 Mr 3 Dewhurst 5 Rev H A Lester Rev T Cook J H Rey Wilfrid Stanton Mrs Howard Mrs Beamont lO3 3 Mr P 0 Price 1 Mr Abdey Mr W Scotson, junr. Mr J Charlton Parr lOO 0 Rev B J Willcocks* 5 0 Mr Walter Ashley Mr Thomas Lloyd 0 1 0 Mr T H Lyon 25 0 Rev J/I Stevenson 2 0 Training College Offertory J G Craik 5 0 Mr R T Harding Mr William Watson 1 0 Mrs Brundrett The Rector Mrs Woods 2 0 Mr S Davies fdr W B Atkin Mr Peter Stubs 5O 0 Mrs Sharp 1,023 1 10 00UNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— TO CONTRACTORS, The Paving and Sewerage Committee Of the Council of the Borough of Warrington Is Prepared to receive TENDERS for FORMING and PAVING the following SIREETS and PASSAGES : Passages between 4to 72. Dudley-street, and 108 to 168. Forster-street. Passage behind 110 and 112, Forster-street. Pickmere-street (footpaths). Thewlis,street (from Baxter-street to new schools). Passage behind open land and Nos. 338 and 310, Liverpool. road Passage along gable of 306, Liverpool-road. Passage behind 296 to 306, Liverpool-road. Richardson's-row (footpath), rear of 1 to 11. Richardson's-row. Richardson s-row (footpath). rear of 2 to 12. Passage behind 250 to 258, Liverpool-road. Passage behind 262 to 256, Liverpool-road. Passage behind 2 to 18, Hepherd- street. Passage behind 210 to 220, Liverpool-road. Passage between 5 and 7, Barnard-street. Drawings, specifications. &amp;c., may be seen, and forms of tender, quantities, and all other information obtained, at the office of the Borough Surveyor, Town Hall, on and after Thursday next, the 25th instant, at which place tenders must be delivered before twelve o'clock on Tuesday,the 6th day of August. 1901. The lowest or any tender not necessarily aocepted. THOMAS LONGDIN, Borough Engineer and Surveyor. Town Hall, Warrington. 19th July. 1901. COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— TO PITCH BOILER MAKERS. The Paving and Sewerage Committee of the Council of the Borough of Warrington Is prepared to receive TENDERS for PITCH BOILER. All further information call be obtained at the office of the Borough Sutveyor, Town Hall. on and after Monday next, the 22nd Inst, at which place tenders must be delivered on or before Twelve o'clock on Monday, the 29th inst. The lowest or any tender not necessarily accepted, THOS. LONGDIN, Borough Engineer and Surveyor, Borough Engineer and Surveyor's, Office, July 19th, 1931.</p>
